==Vietnamese==

===Etymology===
{{vi-etym-sino|心|hv=n||tâm}}. {{doublet|vi|tâm}}.

For some examples of ‹i› in vernacular loans versus ‹â› in standard Sino-Vietnamese, see also {{m|vi|phím}}, {{m|vi|kịp}}, {{m|vi|kín}}, {{m|vi|nhịn}}.

The figurative usage of the word "heart" seen in Modern Vietnamese is at least partially due to foreign influence (either {{ncog|zh|-}} {{ltc-l|心}} or some European languages like {{ncog|fr|cœur}}). Traditionally, the locations for psychological states and feelings are {{m|vi|bụng||belly, abdomen}}, {{m|vi|lòng||intestines, entrails}}, {{m|vi|dạ||stomach, the inside}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{vi-IPA}}

===Noun===
{{vi-noun|cls=[[quả]], [[trái]], [[con]]|[[𢙭]], [[心]]}}

# {{lb|vi|anatomy|cardiology}} a [[heart]]
#* {{quote-book|vi|year=1983|author=Homer|title=Ô-đi-xê|trans-title=The Odyssey|translator=Phan Thị Miến|text=Hẳn là các vị thần trên núi Ô-lem-pơ đã ban cho nàng một trái '''tim''' sắt đá hơn ai hết trong đám đàn bà yếu đuối,{{nb...}}|t=The Olympians must have granted you the hardest '''heart''' among the frail women,{{nb...}}}}

